WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.610
In 1970, airlines carried 310.4
million passengers worldwide.

2
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.630
By 2019, about 14 times as many.

3
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:15.410
In 2005, 15.6 percent of
people used the internet.

4
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.950
By 2025, an estimated 73.6 percent.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.630
The world seems to have shrunk.

6
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.150
So why do most people who
move stay close to home?

7
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.630
Can't they afford a ticket?

8
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.450
Don't they want to go online?

9
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.550
In this mission, you'll
pin down where places are,

10
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:37.110
and trace the flows of goods,
people and information between them.

11
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.490
Then you'll test the shrinking
world against real moving data,

12
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.490
and see why it has shrunk more
for some places than others.

13
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:49.320
Your mission: find out why most people
who move still stay close to home.
